00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:46.450
And these are even diabetics.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.279
They're looking at this problem very superficially.

00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:55.189
It's kind of like if you stub your toe, and
well here, just take a pain pill every time

00:01:55.189 --> 00:01:56.459
you stub your toe.

00:01:56.459 --> 00:02:00.340
But like, why don't we just look at why you're
stubbing your toe in the same spot?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:08.729
The why is this: if you're taking medication
and it's spiking it ... insulin too high and

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:14.890
your blood sugars are coming down too fast,
it could be that you're taking too much medication.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:16.650
You just need to lessen the medication.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:21.819
Rather than try to correct it at the blood
sugar level to add more sugar into the mix

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:27.189
which will create more problem, why not just
take a little less next time to even it out.

00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:28.720
That's one solution.

