00:03:08.819 --> 00:03:12.500
It's called glucagon.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:18.719
Glucagon, okay?

00:03:18.719 --> 00:03:21.010
So that kind of does the opposite of insulin.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:28.110
So if insulin lowers blood sugars, glucagon
raises blood sugars.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:35.280
What it does is it mobilizes and releases
stored sugar from your liver and even the

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.280
muscles.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.099
So you have this thing called glycogen that's
stored sugar, glucagon releases that to keep

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:41.700
the sugars constant.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:47.560
You have this constant thing where your insulin
and glucagon are working together, all right?

